# borrow-doctest

The `run_scoped` doc test that must not compile, copied from scope 0.2.2, next to three variants of it.
Pinned to scope 0.2.2.

    cd proofs/borrow-doctest && cargo test --doc

All 4 pass. The one that matters is

    test src/lib.rs - legal_borrow_untyped_closure (line 28) - compile fail ... ok

That is a legal borrow, with the closure written the way the 0.2.2 test writes it (`move |_cx|`), and it
does not compile either. So the 0.2.2 test passes whether the borrow is legal or not.

What each version of the code fails with (stable rustc 1.97.1):

    cargo build --example as_written          # 5 errors: E0597, and 4 "implementation of `FnOnce`/`FnMut` is not general enough"
    cargo build --example legal_untyped       # 4 errors: the same 4 "not general enough", no E0597
    cargo build --example no_borrow_untyped   # 4 errors: the same 4, with no borrow at all
    cargo build --example illegal_typed       # 1 error: E0597
    cargo run --example legal_typed           # prints completed=1

Plain `cargo test` also builds the examples, and four of them are meant not to compile.
